        "market_blurb": "Cayce, South Carolina sits along the Congaree River directly across from Columbia and has long been a transportation and energy hub, anchored by Dominion Energy's South Carolina headquarters and active CSX rail lines. The local economy blends industrial and logistics operations with retail corridors and public-sector employment tied to Lexington County schools and city government. Its proximity to Columbia also supports a strong base of commuter households and small service businesses.",
        "local_note": "Fire ants, subterranean and occasional Formosan termites, cockroaches, and mosquitoes are the most persistent problems given Cayce's humid Midlands climate, with carpenter ants and wasps also common around older riverside homes. Pest pressure is strongest from spring through fall but termites and ants remain active nearly year-round due to mild winters.",
